; E168 Phase 12, G6(ii) -- MUST NOT COMPILE.
;
; A cap that an observation merely CONSUMED would serve exactly one observation
; and a gate needs many, so every arm of `ObsR` hands a fresh one back and every
; holder must thread it on. This def takes the cap and returns without it. The
; checker refuses the DROP, which is what makes "the run built exactly these
; programs" a fact of the type rather than a claim in a comment -- and it does so
; on the declared binder quantity alone, with no borrowed handle involved.
;
; The compiling twin is e168_cap_thread.chiral, which threads its cap to a
; discharge in every leaf.
;
; want: exit 1, `load: linear binder usage mismatch`

(import "evidence/test-floor")

(def observe-leak (=> (1 bld Builder) Str I64)
  (lam (bld path) 0))

(def compile-main (-> I64 I64) (lam (n) 0))
